  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Kinetic Typography**\n\nI\'m focusing now on crafting a truly special and memorable kinetic typography interaction for \"NOVA.\" The user wants the letters O and V to be interactive, so I\'m trying to visualize a design that feels magical and bespoke, not just a generic effect. I am considering making the interaction tactile.\n\n\n**Exploring Letter Interactions**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in the O and V interaction. The core concept is developing around a physical response. The `O`, envisioned as a lustrous orb, will nudge towards the `V` upon hover. The `V` itself is now conceptualized as a cradle, nest, or valley. The real design challenge now is choreographing the interaction when the `O` rolls into the `V`, ideally with some sort of a soft nest-like magnetic kiss to the cradle. I have several visual concepts for this!\n\n\n**Visualizing Letter Movement**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the Pearl-in-Cradle interaction. Option B feels promising, so I\'m focusing on the choreography of O rolling into V. The V will dip, catch the O with a spring, and a champagne spark will appear. I\'m visualizing the resting state of NOVA being identical to the original wordmark, for a seamless transition.\n\n\n**Refining the Interaction**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction\'s precise timing and visual cues. On hover, the N and A will subtly shift to create space. The O will spin, rise, and glide, its color shifting to champagne. The V will lean to meet it. During contact, the O will drop into the V\'s valley, and there will be a gentle cradle bounce to enhance the feel.\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Cues**\n\nI\'m now implementing the fine details of the interaction. On initial hover, the V compresses and rotates, while the O does a full rotation and scaling. Upon contact, there is an elastic spring in the V and the delicate champagne starburst appears. Hovering over the O or V independently triggers direct letter interactions, and all reset on mouse leave.\n\n\n**Confirming Animation Refinement**\n\nNow, I\'m verifying the smooth reset. After the delightful interaction, all four letters now gracefully glide back to their starting typography effortlessly. The starburst fades away cleanly. I\'ve also confirmed that hovering anywhere over the \"NOVA\" triggers the initial choreographed interaction. Distinct reciprocal physics is present when hovering on O versus V, as intended. I\'m now exploring if the interactive wordmark should be used in both the hero and the header for brand consistency.\n\n\n**Confirming Header Consistency**\n\nI\'m now integrating the interactive wordmark into both the hero and the header to ensure brand consistency. I\'m tailoring the accent colors for optimal contrast; the dark hero film will use a warm champagne hue, while the alabaster header will feature a rich antique gold. I\'m also ensuring accessibility, including screen reader support, aria labels and attributes, and considering reduced motion preferences. I\'ll maintain test IDs for all individual elements.\n\n\n**Validating Accessibility & Code**\n\nI\'m now focusing on accessibility and ensuring clean code. I\'m prioritizing reduced motion preferences, using gentle color glows instead of spinning animations. I\'ve extracted the letter transform choreography into a helper file with unit tests to keep things decoupled and readable. I am writing a verification plan that will ensure all states are tested with the new helper.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "snYCa_OaCZGnqtsP6f-jwQQ"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11642324025407117569"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type NovaInteractionMode = \'idle\' | \'word\' | \'o-nudge\' | \'v-lift\';\\n\\nexport interface LetterTransform {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  rotate: number;\\n  scaleX: number;\\n  scaleY: number;\\n  accented: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SparkleTransform {\\n  opacity: number;\\n  scale: number;\\n  rotate: number;\\n  y: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface NovaWordmarkPose {\\n  N: LetterTransform;\\n  O: LetterTransform;\\n  V: LetterTransform;\\n  A: LetterTransform;\\n  sparkle: SparkleTransform;\\n}\\n\\nconst REST_LETTER: LetterTransform = {\\n  x: 0,\\n  y: 0,\\n  rotate: 0,\\n  scaleX: 1,\\n  scaleY: 1,\\n  accented: false,\\n};\\n\\nconst REST_SPARKLE: SparkleTransform = {\\n  opacity: 0,\\n  scale: 0.2,\\n  rotate: -45,\\n  y: 4,\\n};\\n\\n/**\\n * Pure choreography solver for the interactive NOVA wordmark.\\n * Defines how O (the rolling pearl) and V (the sculptural cradle) physically\\n * interact across hover states while N and A frame the motion gracefully.\\n */\\nexport function getNovaWordmarkPose(\\n  mode: NovaInteractionMode,\\n  reducedMotion = false\\n): NovaWordmarkPose {\\n  if (mode === \'idle\') {\\n    return {\\n      N: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      O: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      V: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      A: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      sparkle: { ...REST_SPARKLE },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (reducedMotion) {\\n    return {\\n      N: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      O: { ...REST_LETTER, accented: true },\\n      V: { ...REST_LETTER, accented: true },\\n      A: { ...REST_LETTER },\\n      sparkle: { opacity: 0.9, scale: 1, rotate: 0, y: 0 },\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  switch (mode) {\\n    case \'word\':\\n      // Hovering NOVA as a whole: O rolls clockwise into the open cradle of V,\\n      // V tilts warmly to catch O, and N/A step slightly outward for balance.\\n      return {\\n        N: { x: -2.5, y: 0, rotate: -2, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        O: { x: 6.5, y: -5.5, rotate: 210, scaleX: 0.96, scaleY: 0.96, accented: true },\\n        V: { x: -2.5, y: 2.5, rotate: 9, scaleX: 1.05, scaleY: 0.94, accented: true },\\n        A: { x: 2.5, y: 0, rotate: 2, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        sparkle: { opacity: 1, scale: 1.05, rotate: 25, y: -7 },\\n      };\\n\\n    case \'o-nudge\':\\n      // Hovering directly on O: O rolls forward and playfully bumps V like Newton\'s cradle,\\n      // causing V to lean right and cushion the impact.\\n      return {\\n        N: { x: -3, y: 0, rotate: -3, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        O: { x: 9.5, y: -3, rotate: 360, scaleX: 1.06, scaleY: 0.94, accented: true },\\n        V: { x: 2.5, y: 3, rotate: 16, scaleX: 0.96, scaleY: 1.04, accented: true },\\n        A: { x: 4, y: 0, rotate: 4, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        sparkle: { opacity: 1, scale: 1.2, rotate: 45, y: -9 },\\n      };\\n\\n    case \'v-lift\':\\n      // Hovering directly on V: V tilts inward and springs upward to toss O\\n      // into a graceful buoyant arc right above its notch.\\n      return {\\n        N: { x: -2.5, y: 0, rotate: -2, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        O: { x: 5.5, y: -11, rotate: -195, scaleX: 1.02, scaleY: 1.04, accented: true },\\n        V: { x: -3.5, y: -2, rotate: -14, scaleX: 1.08, scaleY: 0.95, accented: true },\\n        A: { x: 3, y: 0, rotate: 3, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, accented: false },\\n        sparkle: { opacity: 1, scale: 1.15, rotate: -30, y: -12 },\\n      };\\n  }\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create pure choreography solver for interactive NOVA O-and-V hover poses\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/wordmarkMotion.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating wordmark motion choreography module\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create wordmarkMotion.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\365O\n\362O\001i\024}\023\2613\263z4%GvC\262h\241\333\004\377\033\234\346(\250\035?\307\372\317L\'~}\2100\371\2146\005J$\337\314\360\365\b\225^\325x\031\220)\bs9D\323Y\3420\363\224LC\263F\205\375\031\271\273\0312y\025\n+\313\016ps[\r.\340\317Q\372\363\017Iqi\357\361\275M\2670\306\202{\251\000y\376kx\023\a\177>\367w\177\024\325\342\275\322\030\350\333SE\316\006\276\001\205\365\266<*\n]A\025\"<\2274Q\034$v>\363H\304\363\304\335\026\'\254\333\255\316zBKL\217\215%[\245\323L\324\342\255\264M\'>+\367Tz\242\233\341\362\225\364\030\272\246\240\t\232RCH\343\026\200f\271\240\032\3676\204h\365\020\036e\271L\003m\275\2730{th\320\243\271\216\220\265\261\n\276>\032\250r*\264\225\257\366\002}})r1\342\366\032\353\366\361+N\217\305\374\220\314e#s[\213\347\t-z\035\367\310Ym\0319h\213\027\227\035#\317\305\230\371\213\323\263\267d\234B\256\222&b\343aT#\210\bD\025\215\323\262\363\320\024P\027\346\276\215\332\224\347GP_\272r\312\033\\\333\252T\0308{\\\211\241f\025\346\347:\331\215\234w\021\253w\344\225_\251\363e\204\036\2226`F\017W\323_Q\3116}\371\225 \b+u\2556\312\025D\204\263-\316\240\317\335@\335\032\237UB&%\233\367\025\240)\203L{IFA\366\332\310\227:*\322f\202\351NQ\201P\bE[\036\323\002\245a=\310\330\276t\036*;\230\031Mv\340k\177iNyzD/sw\334\364\376\016]\331\304\361z4\2045.*g\243\251\343\322\340V\302\204\341v\222\241\275\220\'\226\250y \371\277\272\340\270\177\241\3772o6\201Y\271\ro\236\305oG\270\005\267]\036)\365\213\227\327@\346\016\214\231y\213\326\335,\354\203\253\302\311 rSS\220B\320&kb\313.\277\372\235\3418-\223e\346\n\370N\n\357J^Y_a\032\325\277\264\033\342\332\245-\231\314\'\202\354\225\024\257\t\253\313k\371\333f\324\250\317e93-\226\360`\217e\376\235\373\373Y\300\f\266Kn\bq\0253\206I\2458\023F\370\314\251\2009\225\227\223\006]\240\344\352\347\214\331\255\3029\354\271\023;\210\266\337\244\rm\004-I+\237\377\003\223\357Y-\267\\4\253MZ;[iT\377t/\242EX%\352=\317\220\265:\031\263\355O+]\211i\246^\273\222\265/\230\357\263F>k\n\0217\212\373%\375\363\23