  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining a Detail**\n\nI\'m focusing now on `InteractiveNovaWordmark.tsx`, specifically how `tracking-[0.08em]` functions with inline-block spans. I\'m observing that `letter-spacing` applies to text runs within each span when set on the parent `<a>`, not across the entire text as might be expected. This seems key to understanding the visual effect.\n\n\n**Refining the Spacing**\n\nI\'ve been experimenting with `gap-[0.08em]` on the flex container, instead of `letter-spacing`, and it yields identical spacing between letters in the wordmark, with no awkward trailing space. The `onMouseLeave` events fire correctly in sequence, and adding padding to the letter spans makes hovering fluid. I\'m considering replacing `tracking-[0.08em]` with `gap-[0.08em]` to simplify the code.\n\n\n"
