  planner_response {
    response: " templatetags:\nLet\'s design this Odyss\303\251e-signature rising-curtain page transition (`<PageTransitionCurtain />` + pure state/timing controller in `src/utils/pageTransition.ts` with unit tests!) so it matches `image_ed29f622.png` with 100% visual & kinetic fidelity!\n\nLet\'s examine EVERY detail of `image_ed29f622.png` again:\n1. **Nav active dot & tint on hover / click (`\342\200\242 TREATMENTS`)**:\n   Look at the hero navigation bar in `image_ed29f622.png`:\n   - Right before/during clicking `TREATMENTS`, there is a crisp `4px`/`5px` circular dot (`\342\200\242`) to the left of `TREATMENTS`, and `TREATMENTS` shifts to slate-navy (`#5E6780` / `#18224B` or soft translucent ink) while hovered/transitioning!\n   - Let\'s add a smooth hover/pending indicator dot (`\342\200\242`) on the Opening Horizon Navigation buttons (`Treatments`, `Concerns`, `About`) so hovering or clicking `Treatments` reveals that signature Odyss\303\251e dot (`\342\200\242 TREATMENTS`)!\n2. **The Rising Alabaster Curtain (`#FBF9F5`)**:\n   - Triggered whenever navigating across pages (`home` \342\206\222 `treatments`, `home` \342\206\222 `about`, `treatments` \342\206\222 `home`, etc.) \342\200\224 especially clicking **Treatments** anywhere on the Home page (opening hero nav, sticky header, `Treatments` portal card, `Our Philosophy -> Explore treatments`, closing `Treatments` card, or Footer).\n   - **Choreography (powered by GSAP for butter-smooth 60fps cubic-bezier easing)**:\n     - **0.00s \342\206\222 0.62s (Curtain Rise \342\200\224 exact match to `image_ed29f622.png`!)**:\n       - A full-viewport fixed `#FBF9F5` warm alabaster sheet (`z-50`) rises smoothly from `yPercent: 100` (below bottom edge) to `yPercent: 0` (full screen coverage) with `ease: \'power4.inOut\'`.\n       - Simultaneously, the outgoing `<main>` subtly lifts (`y: -48px`) and softens slightly (`opacity: 0.88`), creating the exact spatial depth where the new alabaster sheet wipes cleanly upward over the hero photo!\n       - Mid-way (`~0.28s\342\200\2230.35s`), the viewport looks *literally identical* to `image_ed29f622.png`: top ~63% shows the NOVA hero (`NOVA`, tagline, `\342\200\242 TREATMENTS ...`), bottom ~37% shows the solid, razor-crisp warm alabaster `#FBF9F5` sheet rising cleanly upward!\n     - **0.62s (Seamless Swap at Peak Coverage)**:\n       - With the `#FBF9F5` sheet completely covering the viewport, we swap `activePage` to `\'treatments\'` (or the target page) and reset `window.scrollTo(0, 0)` instantaneously, kill/refresh GSAP ScrollTrigger cleanly, and set the incoming `<main>` at `y: 40px, opacity: 0`.\n     - **0.66s \342\206\222 1.25s (Curtain Reveal + Incoming Page Editorial Glide-Up)**:\n       - The `#FBF9F5` curtain either smoothly lifts off the top (`yPercent: 0 \342\206\222 -100`, `duration: 0.65`, `ease: \'power4.inOut\'`) OR dissolves cleanly as the incoming Treatments page content glides smoothly upward (`y: 40 \342\206\222 0, opacity: 0 \342\206\222 1`, `duration: 0.68`, `ease: \'power3.out\'`).\n       - Wait \342\200\224 let\'s think which feels even more Odyss\303\251e-authentic when arriving on `#FBF9F5`:\n         If the `#FBF9F5` curtain lifts off the top (`yPercent: 0 \342\206\222 -100`) while `TreatmentsSection` (whose background is also `#FBF9F5`) glides upward from `y: 36px, opacity: 0` \342\206\222 `y: 0, opacity: 1`:\n         - During `0.00s \342\206\222 0.62s`, the bottom `#FBF9F5` sheet wipes up over the dark/photographic hero film (exact match to `image_ed29f622.png`!).\n         - At `0.62s`, the screen is pure `#FBF9F5` stillness for a brief breath (`0.06s`), and the sticky `#FBF9F5` header (`NOVA   MENU  TREATMENTS  CONCERNS  ABOUT   BOOK CONSULTATION`) is already in place underneath.\n         - During `0.68s \342\206\222 1.28s`, the `#FBF9F5` sheet sweeps off the top (`yPercent: -100`) revealing the Treatments header, editorial serif title, tabs, and ritual list gliding effortlessly upward into focus (`y: 36 \342\206\222 0, opacity: 0 \342\206\222 1`)!\n         - Zero flash, zero jarring pop, 100% pure Odyss\303\251e architectural motion!\n       - What about `prefers-reduced-motion`? Skip the slide and swap cleanly immediately (`shouldAnimatePageTransition` returns `false`).\n       - What about navigating to a section on the *same* page (e.g. clicking `Concerns` on Home which scrolls to `#our-approach`)? Do NOT trigger a full page-curtain wipe when staying on the same page \342\200\224 just smooth-scroll to `#our-approach` as before!\n       - What if a user clicks another link mid-transition? Guard against re-entrant race conditions cleanly (cancel any running timeline or ignore duplicate clicks to the already-pending target).\n\nLet\'s also check: in `App.tsx`, remember `Header` has `z-40`, and the opening curtain has `z-50`. Our `<PageTransitionCurtain />` should sit at `z-[60]` (above `Header` so the rising `#FBF9F5` sheet sweeps cleanly over everything without getting stuck behind the header, and then reveals the newly visible compact header smoothly as it exits!).\n\nLet\'s write our **verification plan** (per `ultra-mode` skill):\n- **Unit tests** (`src/utils/pageTransition.test.ts`):\n  - Verify `shouldAnimatePageTransition(currentPage, nextPage, reducedMotion)` returns `true` for cross-page transitions (`home -> treatments`, `treatments -> home`, `home -> about`), returns `false` for same-page clicks (`home -> home`), and returns `false` when `reducedMotion` is `true`.\n  - Verify `getPageTransitionTimings()` provides clean positive durations for rise, hold, and reveal phases.\n- **Browser Journey**:\n  1. Open `http://localhost:3000?autostart=1` at desktop `1440\303\227900`.\n  2. Hover and click `Treatments` in the opening hero horizon nav while recording a `.webm` video (`.playwright-cli/r4-treatments-transition.webm`) AND capturing:\n     - a mid-transition screenshot (`r4-transition-mid.png`, ~300ms after click) to verify the exact rising alabaster `#FBF9F5` sheet over the NOVA hero matching `image_ed29f622.png`!\n     - a settled post-transition screenshot (`r4-treatments-arrived.png`, ~1400ms after click) to verify the Treatments page arrived cleanly at `scrollY === 0`, `data-view=\"treatments\"`, curtain hidden (`data-transition-phase=\"idle\"`), and zero console errors!\n  3. Also click `NOVA` in the header on Treatments to verify transitioning back to Home works cleanly without getting stuck.\n\nLet\'s create `/src/utils/pageTransition.ts`, `/src/utils/pageTransition.test.ts`, and `/src/components/PageTransitionCurtain.tsx` in parallel!"
