  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Critical Captures**\n\nI\'m completely blown away by the recent captures! `part_0`, `part_1`, and `part_2` are revealing some major issues. The video frames from 00:18 to 00:34 are especially crucial. It\'s a huge relief that we ran that browser verification; we\'re catching some significant bugs here!\n\n\n**Examining the Critical Defects**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously watching the video and inspecting the screenshots, and I\'ve identified three critical bugs. The most glaring issue is in `PageTransitionCurtain.tsx`.  Inline styling in React is overriding GSAP\'s animations! Whenever React re-renders `PageTransitionCurtain` after a state change, the transform is being reset to `translate3d(0, 100%, 0)`, and snapping the curtain to the bottom. I\'ve got screenshots in `part_0`, I can point this all out in the video frames!\n\n\n**Pinpointing Defect Origins**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on that `r4-treatments-arrived.png` capture. It\'s now clear: the curtain\'s wiping up instead of down over the Treatments page at 00:22 is a direct result of inline styling overriding the GSAP animations, due to React re-renders. The root cause is inline styling on a GSAP-animated element during a re-render. I\'m thinking a `useLayoutEffect` or initial `gsap.set` is the fix. Also, a subtle scaling of the main element to prevent exposing stage B.\n\n\n**Investigating Visibility Anomalies**\n\nI\'ve got another critical issue: the fading logo! I just noticed the `NOVA` logo in `part_1` is initially faint then clearly appears in the `00:21\342\200\22300:22` to `00:31` video frames. In `Header.tsx`, there\'s a transition that\'s causing this logo fade-in effect. The transition causes the text color to change to navy over 500ms while the menu items have a hardcoded color, hence the fade-in effect.\n\n\n**Confirming Critical Solution**\n\nI\'m now completely certain about the fix for the curtain transition. Frame `00:32` in the video is the key; it perfectly visualizes the rising white sheet which is the exact same color as that `image_ed29f622.png`! Removing that inline transform style and we should have a smooth, clean transition revealing Treatments. This will also make the page transition look exactly like the `image_ed29f622.png` graphic.\n\n\n**Refining Curtain Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on optimizing the curtain transition to perfectly mimic Odyss\303\251e\'s animation. I\'m focusing on three phases: rising, swapping, and revealing. During the rising phase, I\'m thinking of a full-viewport sheet and eliminating main element shifts. Swapping needs instantaneous page change, and the revealing phase requires smooth curtain and main element movement. This approach makes it a clean and precise effect!\n\n\n"
    message_id: "s4ICa7SqIfWM_PUP58W-8AY"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11517571136180164497"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useLayoutEffect } from \'react\';\\nimport gsap from \'gsap\';\\nimport type { TransitionPhase } from \'../utils/pageTransition\';\\n\\ninterface PageTransitionCurtainProps {\\n  curtainRef: React.RefObject<HTMLDivElement | null>;\\n  phase: TransitionPhase;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Full-viewport warm alabaster (#FBF9F5) rising architectural sheet that wipes\\n * cleanly upward from the bottom edge during cross-page navigation (Odyss\303\251e style),\\n * matching the crisp horizontal horizon curtain transition.\\n *\\n * Transform is owned exclusively by GSAP (initialized off-screen on mount)\\n * so React phase re-renders never overwrite the in-flight animation.\\n */\\nexport const PageTransitionCurtain: React.FC<PageTransitionCurtainProps> = ({\\n  curtainRef,\\n  phase,\\n}) => {\\n  const isActive = phase !== \'idle\';\\n\\n  useLayoutEffect(() => {\\n    if (curtainRef.current) {\\n      gsap.set(curtainRef.current, { yPercent: 100 });\\n    }\\n  }, [curtainRef]);\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div\\n      ref={curtainRef}\\n      aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\"\\n      data-testid=\\\"page-transition-curtain\\\"\\n      data-transition-phase={phase}\\n      className={`fixed inset-0 z-[60] bg-[#FBF9F5] will-change-transform ${\\n        isActive ? \'pointer-events-auto\' : \'pointer-events-none\'\\n      }`}\\n    />\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Remove inline transform style from PageTransitionCurtain so React re-renders never reset GSAP animation\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/PageTransitionCurtain.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Fixing PageTransitionCurtain transform ownership\", \"toolSummary\":\"Fix PageTransitionCurtain.tsx\"}"
