  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Mapping Visuals to Structure**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the eleven reference screenshots. My aim is to meticulously map each one directly to **NOVA Unisex Salon**\'s editorial architecture, ensuring a 1-to-1 correlation and preservation of the existing service structure.\n\n\n**Refining Category Definitions**\n\nI\'m now refining the service categories. My current plan involves either four rich salon categories or five if we introduce **Hair Artistry & Unisex Grooming**. The user\'s feedback is key; they want to keep the services but present them engagingly with video/images. Therefore, I must prioritize mapping all sections in the Odyss\303\251e `/treatments` screenshots for treatment-related services. Also, ensuring that ALL EXISTING booking logic and unit tests continue to work is paramount.\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Rhythm**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously analyzing the visual rhythm present in the NOVA Treatments page, as that page achieves an impressive jaw-dropping luxury editorial design. Currently, I\'m focusing on the architectural breakdown across the eleven reference screenshots. The floating bottom-left chapter index is the focal point, encompassing \"TREATMENTS,\" \"OUR SERVICES,\" and \"PRE AND AFTERCARE\" for smooth-scroll navigation. I am paying close attention to the positioning and adaptive color schemes across different sections.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Sections**\n\nI\'m now identifying the key sections for the visual design, starting with a full-viewport opening video. I\'m focusing on incorporating existing assets like the `/videos/approach-2.mp4` for a cinematic feel and `/images/spread-right-texture.jpg` to maintain a luxurious ambiance. Header behavior over the opening video is important; I must keep in mind its color and opacity transitions upon scroll.\n\n\n**Updating Header Transition**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the header transitions as the user scrolls. I need to update `Header.tsx` to handle the switch from luminous ivory over the video on the top to midnight navy on alabaster as soon as the user scrolls past the initial video, and I\'m looking at screenshot 3-4 for reference. The split headline, \"Guided by craft\" and \"refined through care,\" blurs and fades as the sticky video container scrolls.\n\n\n**Defining Section Manifestos**\n\nI\'m now identifying the key sections and manifestos. Focusing on screenshot 3, I\'m integrating the editorial serif manifesto from the lower-right column into a clear statement. I will make sure the user sees a crisp, indented section with the text \"Beauty is a living, unhurried ritual...\" followed by the micro-label \"A TREATMENT PLAN SHAPED FOR YOU\" for a smooth scroll. After that, I will work on Section 2.\n\n\n**Visualizing Chapter Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the scroll-linked service chapters, specifically focusing on screenshots 3-8! I\'m mapping the desktop layout, especially the left half which has a sticky service index and accordion. I am going to need to build that service list with the correct typography and descriptions, so that the index lists all four NOVA salon service categories with Odyss\303\251e\'s exact numbered editorial typography.\n\n\n**Structuring Service Presentation**\n\nI\'m now focused on presenting service data. My current aim involves displaying service names, durations, and prices clearly, separated by `\302\267`, in unboxed metadata. Clicking any ritual should open the Booking Drawer pre-selected to that category and ritual. I also need to render inactive chapters in muted slate-navy with hover effects. Additionally, I need to create the right half using a tall, continuous stack of full-bleed salon photography and film.\n\n\n\n**Mapping Visual Flows**\n\nI am now focusing on the visual flow, especially for screenshots 7 and 8, where full-bleed photos link directly. I plan to use high-res images and looping videos for stacked editorial panels. I\'m focusing on \"Facials,\" \"Manicure,\" \"Makeup,\" and \"Consultation.\" Also, I\'m integrating Scroll Synchronization to trigger visual updates based on the viewport.\n\n\n**Defining Mobile Experience**\n\nI am now focusing on the mobile presentation. For each of the service categories 1-4, I need to ensure that the editorial image is paired directly with its numbered heading, prose, ritual list, and booking action, so that it displays properly even on small screens. Also, service chapter on the sticky left column needs to work. On the left column, clicking on any title should smoothly scroll to its photo and expand its rituals.\n\n\n**Defining Journey Manifest**\n\nI am now focusing on section five, which has an alabaster \"YOUR JOURNEY\" centered pause. I want to build this section using screenshots 10 and 11. I plan to center \"YOUR JOURNEY\" with a quiet, refined \"Book a Consultation\" button so visitors can easily book a session. I need to make sure that \"Artisanal precision, made personal.\" appears right underneath.\n\n\n**Visualizing Editorial Diptych**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the centered diptych in Screenshot 11. I plan to build a narrow, stacked column with two visuals: a macro close-up of skin and a warm hands-on-skin shot. These will flow into the footer with a \"hover scale\" effect and be clickable, and I need to ensure zero gap.\n\n\n**Implementing Scroll Effects**\n\nI\'m now implementing the scroll effects for a smooth transition from the video hero to the monochrome band and centered \"YOUR JOURNEY\" section, keeping all NOVA services and booking logic intact. I\'m focusing on clean, testable helper functions. I\'ve created `src/utils/treatmentsScroll.ts` and `src/utils/treatmentsScroll.test.ts` with helper logic: `resolveTreatmentsHeroStage` for the hero video transition, and `resolveActiveTreatmentsSection` to determine the active section and dark surface. I\'m ensuring everything is deterministic and easily testable.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Transitions**\n\nI\'m now refining the scroll transitions, particularly for the header, ensuring it renders correctly based on the current scroll position and active page. I\'m focusing on making a switch from luminous ivory over the video to midnight navy on alabaster when the user scrolls past the initial video, per the screenshots, ensuring all cases are covered. I\'ve created the helper functions to unit test. I also want to make sure the header behavior 100% unchanged for the home and about pages.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Page Transition**\n\nI\'m now running comprehensive browser verification across desktop and mobile, ensuring smooth page transitions and responsive design. After navigating to the Treatments section, I\'m capturing critical screenshots to verify the hero frame, ethos reveal, and modalities, checking for full-bleed video, correct header color transitions, and the presence of all key visual elements. I\'m rigorously testing the sticky left list and stacked salon media presentation. Additionally, I\'m ensuring all existing tests run without regressions.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "34cCa8vzHdre-sAPmYShqQY"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5103392740309784564"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type TreatmentsAnchorId = \'treatments\' | \'modalities\' | \'aftercare\';\\n\\nexport interface TreatmentsHeroVisualState {\\n  headlineOpacity: number;\\n  headlineBlurPx: number;\\n  manifestoOpacity: number;\\n  manifestoY: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface TreatmentsSectionStatus {\\n  activeAnchor: TreatmentsAnchorId;\\n  isOverDarkMedia: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nfunction clamp01(value: number): number {\\n  return Math.max(0, Math.min(1, value));\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Maps scroll progress (0..1) through the Treatments opening video hero into\\n * the signature Odyss\303\251e dissolve:\\n * - 0.00 -> 0.25: Crisp split headline (\\\"Guided by craft\\\" / \\\"refined through care.\\\")\\n * - 0.25 -> 0.72: Split headline softens/blurs back while right-aligned manifesto rises cleanly\\n * - 0.72 -> 1.00: Manifesto holds legible focus before alabaster modalities enter\\n */\\nexport function resolveTreatmentsHeroStage(\\n  rawProgress: number,\\n  reducedMotion = false\\n): TreatmentsHeroVisualState {\\n  const p = clamp01(rawProgress);\\n\\n  if (reducedMotion) {\\n    return {\\n      headlineOpacity: p < 0.45 ? 1 : 0.35,\\n      headlineBlurPx: 0,\\n      manifestoOpacity: p < 0.35 ? 0 : 1,\\n      manifestoY: 0,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  const dissolve = clamp01((p - 0.14) / 0.42);\\n  const manifestoIn = clamp01((p - 0.24) / 0.38);\\n\\n  return {\\n    headlineOpacity: Number((1 - dissolve * 0.72).toFixed(3)),\\n    headlineBlurPx: Number((dissolve * 3.5).toFixed(2)),\\n    manifestoOpacity: Number(manifestoIn.toFixed(3)),\\n    manifestoY: Number(((1 - manifestoIn) * 34).toFixed(1)),\\n  };\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Determines which bottom-left chapter anchor is active and whether floating\\n * chrome (bottom-left index) currently sits over dark photography/video.\\n */\\nexport function resolveActiveTreatmentsSection(\\n  scrollY: number,\\n  bounds: {\\n    heroHeight: number;\\n    aftercareTop: number;\\n    aftercareBottom: number;\\n  },\\n  viewportHeight: number\\n): TreatmentsSectionStatus {\\n  const probeY = scrollY + viewportHeight * 0.55;\\n  const bottomNavY = scrollY + viewportHeight - 48;\\n\\n  if (probeY < bounds.heroHeight) {\\n    return {\\n      activeAnchor: \'treatments\',\\n      isOverDarkMedia: bottomNavY < bounds.heroHeight,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  if (probeY >= bounds.aftercareTop) {\\n    return {\\n      activeAnchor: \'aftercare\',\\n      isOverDarkMedia:\\n        bottomNavY >= bounds.aftercareTop && bottomNavY <= bounds.aftercareBottom,\\n    };\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    activeAnchor: \'modalities\',\\n    isOverDarkMedia:\\n      bottomNavY >= bounds.aftercareTop && bottomNavY <= bounds.aftercareBottom,\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create pure scroll choreography helpers for the editorial Treatments page\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/treatmentsScroll.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating Treatments scroll choreography helpers\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create treatmentsScroll.ts\"}"
