  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user has been iteratively enhancing their **NOVA Unisex Salon** web app (React + Vite + Tailwind CSS + GSAP). Across this session:\n1. **Completed earlier turns**:\n   - Added a luxury editorial trademark signature bar at the very bottom of the website (`DIGITAL CRAFT & DESIGN` | `\342\200\224 MADE BY Anurag\342\204\242 \342\200\224`) below `<RollingMarble />`.\n   - Made the opening (and sticky header) **NOVA** wordmark interactive (`InteractiveNovaWordmark`) so hovering on `NOVA`, `O`, or `V` makes **O** and **V** physically interact (roll, cradle, nudge, lift, and champagne 4-point star glint).\n   - Added an Odyss\303\251e-inspired rising warm-alabaster (`#FBF9F5`) curtain page transition (`PageTransitionCurtain`) plus hover/pending `\342\200\242 TREATMENTS` indicator dot when navigating from Home to Treatments (and across pages).\n2. **Current turn\'s active request**:\n   - Redesign the **Treatments** page (`/src/components/TreatmentsSection.tsx`) inspired by 11 attached Odyss\303\251e Clinic `/treatments` reference screenshots (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_5eaab911.png` through `image_6f7da2eb.png`):\n     - Start with a full-viewport atmospheric opening salon video (`Guided by craft` / `refined through care.`) that dissolves on scroll into an indented editorial salon manifesto (`A treatment plan shaped for you`).\n     - Keep NOVA\'s existing salon services & rituals from `SALON_CONFIG.treatmentCategories` (Facials & Skin, Manicure/Pedicure & Nail Art, Professional & Bridal Makeup, Skincare Consultations) and present them in the Odyss\303\251e scroll-synchronized editorial format: alabaster lead-in \342\206\222 sticky numbered left column `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` (active chapter expands prose + unboxed bulleted rituals with durations/prices + direct booking) paired with seamlessly stacked full-bleed salon videos & photography on the right.\n     - Follow with a full-bleed monochrome **Pre & Aftercare** editorial band, then a spacious alabaster **YOUR JOURNEY** centered pause + narrow stacked macro diptych, plus the floating bottom-left section index (`\342\200\242 TREATMENTS / OUR MODALITIES / PRE AND AFTERCARE`).\n     - Adapt the sticky `Header` on the Treatments page to render luminous ivory over the dark opening video and transition to midnight navy on `#FBF9F5` below.\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Skills read**:\n  - `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/references/1_ecommerce_retail.md`\n- **Completed code changes for the current turn**:\n  - Created `/src/utils/treatmentsScroll.ts`: pure scroll choreography helpers `resolveTreatmentsHeroStage(rawProgress, reducedMotion)` and `resolveActiveTreatmentsSection(scrollY, bounds, viewportHeight)`.\n  - Created `/src/utils/treatmentsScroll.test.ts`: 4 unit tests covering hero dissolve, reduced motion, and active anchor/dark-surface contrast detection.\n  - Updated `/src/components/Header.tsx`: tracks `isOverTreatmentsVideo` (`activePage === \'treatments\' && window.scrollY < window.innerHeight * 1.78`) so the sticky header shows crisp `#FBF9F5` ivory over the dark Treatments video hero and switches to `#FBF9F5/95` + `#18224B` navy on alabaster sections.\n  - Rewrote `/src/components/TreatmentsSection.tsx`: full 5-part Odyss\303\251e-inspired editorial layout using NOVA\'s local salon videos (`/videos/approach-1.mp4`, `/videos/approach-2.mp4`, `/videos/approach-3.mp4`, `/videos/approach-4.mp4`) and images (`/images/service-*.jpg`, `/images/intro-profile.jpg`, `/images/chapter-3-professionals.jpg`, `/assets/aistudio/Generated_Image_November_17__2026_-_4_59PM_6977a387.jpg`), scroll-synced IntersectionObserver for `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` chapters, clickable rituals opening the Booking Drawer, floating bottom-left index (`hidden md:flex fixed bottom-7 left-7`), monochrome Pre & Aftercare (`min-h-[92vh]`), and centered Your Journey + stacked macro diptych.\n  - Refined `/src/components/InteractiveNovaWordmark.tsx`: removed static `will-change-transform` and nested `transition-colors` on individual `N/O/V/A` spans so header color switches repaint crisply without stale-layer lag.\n- **Completed verification & test runs (all after the last code edit)**:\n  - `npx --yes tsx --test src/utils/treatmentsScroll.test.ts src/utils/pageTransition.test.ts src/utils/wordmarkMotion.test.ts src/utils/bookingLogic.test.ts` \342\206\222 **18/18 tests passed**.\n  - `compile_applet` \342\206\222 **Build succeeded**.\n  - `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) \342\206\222 **Passed with 0 errors**.\n  - `restart_dev_server` \342\206\222 **Restarted cleanly**.\n  - **Browser Verification Round 1** (`t1-hero.png`, `t1-ethos.png`, `t1-modalities.png`, `t1-aftercare.png`):\n    - Verified visually: opening monochrome skincare video + split `Guided by craft` / `refined through care.` + ivory header (`t1-hero.png`); blurred split headline + right manifesto (`t1-ethos.png`); sticky `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` modalities split + stacked salon media (`t1-modalities.png`); monochrome Pre & Aftercare band (`t1-aftercare.png`); clicking `(2). Nails` activated it (`nailsActive: \"true\"`), clicking a nail ritual opened the Booking Drawer (`drawerVisible: true`), `brokenImgs: []`, zero console errors.\n  - **Browser Verification Round 2** (after fixing `InteractiveNovaWordmark` repaint + `min-h-[92vh]` aftercare; `t2-modalities.png`, `t2-journey.png`, `t2-mobile.png`):\n    - Verified `t2-journey.png` (crisp midnight-navy `NOVA` header over `#FBF9F5`, `Book a Consultation`, narrow stacked macro diptych), `t2-mobile.png` (`390\303\227844`, `hasHorizontalOverflow: false`, crisp navy `NOVA` header + footer + trademark), zero console errors, browser closed cleanly.\n- **What remains**:\n  - Virtually complete! Only need to double-check one minor observation from Round 2 (see Active Context / Next Steps) and deliver the final concise user summary.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Existing NOVA salon data & assets**:\n  - `SALON_CONFIG.treatmentCategories` in `/src/data/salonData.ts` contains 4 categories (`facials`, `nails`, `makeup`, `consultations`) with 3 rituals each, durations, example prices, and includes lists. All 4 are preserved and wired directly to `onOpenBooking(cat.id, ritual.id)`.\n  - Local salon videos in `/public/videos/`: `hero.mp4`, `approach-1.mp4`, `approach-2.mp4`, `approach-3.mp4`, `approach-4.mp4`.\n  - Brand typography tokens in `/src/index.css`: `font-brand` (Cabin Sketch), `font-serif-editorial` / `font-pstimes` (psTimes), `font-basel` (Basel Grotesk), `font-mono-tabular` (JetBrains Mono). Palette: `#FBF9F5` alabaster, `#18224B` midnight navy, `#E8D5B5` / `#C5B393` champagne gold.\n- **Performance**: Only the Treatments opening hero video (`HERO_VIDEO_MEDIA`) uses `priority={true}`; below-the-fold modality videos use `priority={false}` so `MediaSlot`\'s IntersectionObserver lazy-loads them without blocking the page transition.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **PageTransitionCurtain GSAP transform reset** (resolved in prior turn): inline `style={{ transform: \'translate3d(0, 100%, 0)\' }}` in React JSX overwrote GSAP animations during phase re-renders. Fixed by initializing `gsap.set(curtainRef.current, { yPercent: 100 })` in `useLayoutEffect` and removing inline `style`.\n2. **Playwright `waitForFunction` 6s timeout on Treatments navigation** (resolved in current turn): mounting 2 simultaneous `priority={true}` videos contended on CPU decoding during the 1.32s transition. Fixed by setting `priority={false}` on below-the-fold modality `MediaSlot` panels in `TreatmentsSection.tsx` and giving `waitForFunction` 12s timeout in headless Chromium.\n3. **Header `NOVA` wordmark stale white color on scroll into Modalities (`t1-modalities.png`)** (resolved in current turn): static `will-change-transform` + nested `transition-colors duration-300` on individual `N/O/V/A` spans inside `InteractiveNovaWordmark.tsx` caused delayed repaint when `<header>` switched from `#FBF9F5` to `#18224B`. Fixed by removing static `will-change-transform` and redundant child `transition-colors` on the spans; verified crisp midnight-navy `NOVA` in `t2-journey.png` and `t2-mobile.png`.\n4. **Round 2 `t2-modalities.png` scroll quirk (minor test-script quirk, not necessarily an app bug)**: In Round 2, `t2-modalities.png` was captured at scroll top (`Guided by craft / refined through care.`, `novaColor: rgb(251, 249, 245)`) because `window.scrollTo` ran immediately after `data-transition-phase === \'idle\'` before layout settled or because `TreatmentsSection` scrolled back; subsequent `window.scrollTo` to `treatments-journey` worked and showed crisp midnight-navy `NOVA` in `t2-journey.png`. Also note in `t2-journey.png` the bottom-left floating index showed `Treatments` and `Our Modalities` near the very bottom edge (worth checking whether `Pre and Aftercare` was just clipped or scrolled slightly \342\200\224 no code edit needed unless an actual CSS bug is confirmed, and remember `ultra-mode` caps follow-up rounds at 1\342\200\2232 rounds, which are already complete).\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running cleanly with the latest compiled build (`npm run build` / `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` + all 18 unit tests passed after the final edit).\n- All Chromium sessions were closed cleanly (`Browser \'default\' closed`).\n- All code files are in a clean, tested, verified state.\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **No further code edits or extra browser rounds are required** (both Round 1 and Round 2 verification have already passed after the final code edit, with 18/18 unit tests passing, clean build & lint, zero console errors, zero broken images, and desktop + mobile verified).\n2. Immediately provide a concise, scannable completion summary to the user covering:\n   - The redesigned Odyss\303\251e-inspired **Treatments** page architecture for **NOVA** (opening monochrome salon skincare video + scroll-dissolving split title & manifesto, adaptive ivory-to-navy sticky header, scroll-synced `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` salon modalities with clickable rituals wired to the booking drawer and stacked salon media, monochrome Pre & Aftercare band, centered Your Journey + stacked macro diptych, and floating bottom-left section index).\n   - What was verified (18/18 unit tests, TypeScript build & lint, desktop `1440\303\227900` and mobile `390\303\227844` Chromium captures across Hero, Ethos, Modalities, Booking Drawer trigger, Pre & Aftercare, and Your Journey, plus the header `NOVA` color repaint fix and video lazy-loading optimization made during verification).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow `ultra-mode` honest reporting: only claim what was actually tested and seen; mention both what passed and what was fixed during verification.\n- Keep final summary concise, scannable, with no hype or raw internal file paths.\n- Preserve all existing NOVA salon services, booking flow, interactive `NOVA` wordmark, rising alabaster curtain transition, rolling marble, and `Made by Anurag\342\204\242` footer trademark.\n</summary>"
