  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Anticipating CSS Edge Cases**\n\nI\'ve hit a potential snag with the `maskGradient`. Specifically, it concerns the incoming slide\'s mask gradient when `translateYPercent` is above zero. I\'m focusing on the interaction between the slide div\'s existing `transform` style and the application of `maskGradient`. A careful examination is ongoing to find the potential problem before we even get to the testing phase.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mask Application**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining how `maskImage` interacts with transforms. Specifically, I\'ve confirmed that the mask gradient applies within the *local* coordinate box of the masked element. I\'m working through the math for various `translateYPercent` and `scale` values to understand the exact positioning of the mask edge in relation to the parent\'s `overflow: hidden`. I\'m also now considering the `visibility: hidden` property and how it affects the `IntersectionObserver`, which is good since I\'ve found it doesn\'t affect visibility.\n\n\n"
