  planner_response {
    response: "The right-hand media column on the **Treatments** page now uses a scroll-driven **vanishing editorial deck** so each salon video and photograph smoothly scrolls into the next while the previous frame dissolves away.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Sticky Vanishing Media Stage (Desktop)**: Replaced the static vertical stack on desktop with a pinned editorial frame paired beside the sticky `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` modalities column.\n- **Scroll-Into-One-Another & Vanishing Choreography**:\n  - As you scroll down from one chapter to the next, the **outgoing video/photo** softly recedes in scale, drifts upward, blurs out of focus, and fades into the warm `#FBF9F5` alabaster canvas.\n  - Simultaneously, the **incoming video/photo** glides upward into the same frame through a soft feathered gradient mask with a subtle optical settle, melting seamlessly through the vanishing visual beneath.\n  - Scrolling back up reverses the transition symmetrically, and `prefers-reduced-motion` switches to a calm crossfade without blur or displacement.\n- **Synchronized Chapter Navigation**: Scrolling automatically activates the matching `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` chapter on the left at the transition midpoint, and clicking any chapter button smoothly scrolls the deck straight to that service\342\200\231s crisp settled stop. Mobile continues to display each paired visual cleanly inline under the expanded chapter.\n\n### Verified\n- **Unit Tests**: 22/22 tests passed, including new tests for the vanishing deck\342\200\231s start/end settled states, mid-scroll outgoing/incoming blend physics, reduced-motion fallback, and chapter scroll-target alignment.\n- **Build & Type Check**: Production build and TypeScript lint passed with zero errors.\n- **Browser Check (`1440\303\227900` Chromium)**: Verified navigating from Home to Treatments, settled `(1). Facials` frame, mid-scroll vanishing blend where `(1).` softly recedes and blurs as `(2).` flows up into it, clicking `(3). Professional and bridal makeup` to jump cleanly to the settled third visual, and clicking a ritual item to open the Booking Drawer\342\200\224with zero console errors and zero broken images. (Continuous motion was verified via settled and mid-transition captures rather than a `.webm` recording.)"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visuals\' Impact**\n\nI\'m incredibly captivated by the screenshots, especially `vanish-midblend.png`. The visual impact is simply stunning! My focus is now on the nuances of this image. It\'s a key part of the whole thing! I\'m really digging into the details!\n\n\n"
