    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial Failure**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause of the initial failure: `menu-desktop.png` is missing! This means the issue occurred right at the first `Menu` click. My focus is now on why the initial click failed to open the `MenuDrawer`. I\'m going to meticulously review `MenuDrawer.tsx`, `Header.tsx`, and `TreatmentsSection.tsx` to understand the sequence of events and identify the point of breakage.\n\n\n**Tracing the Button Click**\n\nI\'m now tracing the exact sequence after the Menu button click. The script successfully clicked the button, which is confusing. The timeout occurred on `waitForSelector(\'[data-testid=nova-menu-drawer][data-state=open]\')`. I suspect a timing issue related to server restarts or the component lifecycle, specifically in `Header.tsx` and `MenuDrawer.tsx`. The `setMenuOpen(true)` call in `Header.tsx` seems to trigger the rendering of `MenuDrawer` with `isOpen={true}`, however the component may not be fully rendered, blocking the test execution. I\'ll focus on the rendering process.\n\n\n**Investigating Visibility States**\n\nI\'m now investigating visibility and rendering states. My focus shifted to `Header.tsx`, specifically line 63. I initially suspected an issue in `MenuDrawer.tsx` with rendering, but now I\'m looking into the visibility changes. The header\'s classes manage transitions, opacity, and positioning. I suspect the animation\'s timing could be affecting the test.\n\n\n**Uncovering StrictMode Problem**\n\nI\'ve got it! I think I\'ve found a React StrictMode issue in `MenuDrawer`. I\'ve been tracing the `isOpen` change and how it affects rendering. I think a strict mode double mount is causing issues with the render. This could be blocking the test execution. I\'ve been examining the `useEffect` hook in `MenuDrawer.tsx`, and the way the `data-testid` is rendered, and think I\'m closing in on it.\n\n\n"
