  planner_response {
    response: "The **Book Consultation** experience has been transformed from a compact side form into a full-viewport, two-panel **NOVA Consultation Sanctuary**.\n\n### What Changed\n- **Live Atmospheric Ritual Canvas (Left Panel / Mobile Top Banner)**:\n  - Plays a full-bleed salon film that crossfades dynamically whenever you switch between **Facials & Skin**, **Nails & Manicure**, **Makeup & Bridal**, and **Consultations**.\n  - Displays a live **Ritual Dossier** over the film showing the active ritual\342\200\231s title, summary, included steps, duration, sample fee, and your chosen date & time window as you build your booking.\n- **Guided 3-Step Alabaster Concierge Flow**:\n  - **01. Ritual**: Tactile modality selector tabs and selectable editorial ritual cards replace standard dropdowns, with a hairline progress bar along the sticky top bar.\n  - **02. Schedule**: One-tap upcoming date tiles (`Mon`\342\200\223`Sat`), a custom future date picker, and an architectural time-window grid.\n  - **03. Guest Details**: Live summary strip with a quick `Modify` shortcut, refined underline typography inputs, and one-tap sanctuary preference tags (`Quiet silent ritual`, `Sensitive skin`, `Bridal timeline`, `Fragrance-free`) that toggle cleanly into your notes.\n- **Letterpress Confirmation Invitation**: Completing the form transitions into a framed **NOVA Sanctuary Dossier** confirmation card showing your reference code, ritual details, arrival window, notes, and Lucknow studio address, while preserving saved session requests.\n\n### Verified\n- **Unit Tests**: 25/25 tests passed, including new tests for step-scoped validation, upcoming date generation, and preference tag toggling.\n- **Build & Type Check**: Production build and TypeScript lint passed with zero errors.\n- **Browser Check (Desktop `1440\303\227900` & Mobile `390\303\227844` Chromium)**: Verified opening the full-viewport sanctuary, switching to **Makeup & Bridal** (confirming live film & dossier updates), Step 2 validation when advancing without a date, picking a date tile and `02:30 PM` slot, Step 3 empty-submit validation, completing guest details with `Quiet silent ritual`, reaching the letterpress confirmation card (`REF \302\267 MA-AN1124`), and checking the mobile layout\342\200\224with zero console errors and zero horizontal overflow."
    thinking: "**Inspecting Initial Impressions**\n\nOkay, wow! I\'m completely blown away by the initial visuals across all the screenshots. It\'s giving me serious Awwwards-winning Parisian luxury editorial vibes, particularly on the desktop. The mobile view looks equally impressive. I\'m excited to delve deeper into each step.\n\n\n**Analyzing Booking Flow**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the booking flow. The first desktop frame presents a strong visual narrative, with a high-quality salon video on the left and a sophisticated concierge interface on the right. The progression through the hairline visual feedback makes it easy to follow the steps of the flow, with date and time selection offering great utility. I will need to inspect the interface and modality cards.\n\n\n**Reviewing Confirmed Booking Flow**\n\nI\'ve carefully examined the \"booking-confirmed-desktop.png\" screenshot. I\'m especially impressed by the luxury letterpress design of the NOVA Sanctuary Dossier card. The champagne gold border, reference number, and clear presentation of ritual details are excellent. The mobile view is also impressive, with its cinematic banner and step cards. There\'s zero clipping and no horizontal overflow, with clear steps for the mobile user.\n\n\n"
