    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user has been iteratively refining their **NOVA Unisex Salon** web app (React + Vite + Tailwind CSS + GSAP). Across recent turns:\n1. **Completed prior turns**:\n   - Redesigned the **Treatments** page with an Odyss\303\251e-inspired scroll-choreographed opening video, adaptive ivory-to-navy header, sticky `(1).`\342\200\223`(4).` modalities, monochrome Pre & Aftercare band, Your Journey diptych, and bottom-left floating section index.\n   - Upgraded the right-hand desktop media on **Treatments** into a scroll-driven **vanishing editorial deck** (`resolveModalityDeckState` + feathered gradient mask) so each salon video/photo scrolls smoothly into the next while the outgoing visual recedes, blurs, and vanishes.\n   - Redesigned the **Menu** overlay into a right-side frosted blurred editorial drawer (`/src/components/MenuDrawer.tsx`) with top-left `CLOSE`, `1.`\342\200\223`5.` serif links, portrait + craft philosophy note, and bottom `#18224B` `A.`/`C.`/`S.` contact block.\n   - Redesigned **Book Consultation** (`/src/components/BookingDrawer.tsx`) into a full-viewport two-panel consultation sanctuary (left live crossfading salon film + live ritual dossier, right 3-step guided concierge flow + letterpress confirmation card).\n   - Removed all remaining legacy **Maison Aura** / `MA-` references across `salonData.ts`, `bookingLogic.ts`, `bookingLogic.test.ts`, `Header.tsx`, `MenuDrawer.tsx`, and `index.html`, standardizing on **NOVA** (`The NOVA Signature Facial`, `NOVA-\342\200\246` reference codes, `NOVA \342\200\224 Unisex Salon & Beauty Sanctuary`).\n2. **Current turn\'s active request**:\n   - The user attached `/public/assets/aistudio/image_30c907b5.png` (showing the Odyss\303\251e hero horizon bar with `\342\227\217 TREATMENTS` hovered in crisp midnight navy `#18224B` with a solid circular dot to the left of the text while neighboring links stay luminous white with zero layout shift) and asked:\n     *\"see when i hover how these changes make the same for this app\"*\n\n## 2. Progress\n- **Skills read**:\n  - `/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`\n  - `/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`\n- **Completed code changes for the current turn**:\n  - Created `/src/components/NavHoverLink.tsx`: reusable navigation link button implementing the exact Odyss\303\251e hover interaction with **zero layout shift** (an absolutely positioned `5.5px` solid circular dot at `-left-3.5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2` that smoothly scales & fades in on hover, keyboard focus-visible, or active route).\n    - `variant=\"hero\"`: transitions from crisp luminous ivory (`#FBF9F5`) to pure deep midnight navy (`#18224B`, removing dark text shadow on hover so the navy stays razor-sharp) with a solid `#18224B` dot.\n    - `variant=\"header-light\"`: midnight navy `#18224B` label + `#18224B` dot on the alabaster sticky header and footer directory links.\n    - `variant=\"header-dark-video\"`: luminous ivory `#FBF9F5` transitioning to champagne gold `#E8D5B5` + `#E8D5B5` dot over the dark monochrome Treatments opening video so contrast remains high.\n  - Updated `/src/App.tsx`: applied `NavHoverLink` (`variant=\"hero\"`) across all four Home Opening Horizon Navigation links (`Treatments`, `Concerns`, `About`, `Book Consultation`) and moved the parent container\'s `drop-shadow` onto only the wordmark and tagline so hovered `#18224B` text is never muddied by a dark shadow.\n  - Updated `/src/components/Header.tsx`: applied `NavHoverLink` across sticky header links (`Menu`, `Treatments`, `Concerns`, `About`, `Book Consultation`), replacing the old underline active state with the signature `\342\227\217` dot.\n  - Updated `/src/components/Footer.tsx`: applied `NavHoverLink` across the footer quick directory links (`Home`, `Treatments`, `About`, `Book Consultation`).\n- **Completed verification & checks (all run after the final code edit)**:\n  - `compile_applet` \342\206\222 **Build succeeded**.\n  - `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`) \342\206\222 **Passed with 0 errors**.\n  - `restart_dev_server` \342\206\222 **Restarted cleanly**.\n  - **Browser Verification (`1440\303\227900` Chromium)** via `playwright-cli` (`http://localhost:3000?autostart=1`):\n    - Captured `.playwright-cli/nav-hover-hero.png` while hovering `TREATMENTS` in the Opening Horizon Navigation: visually verified **`\342\227\217 TREATMENTS`** renders in crisp deep midnight navy (`#18224B`) with a clean solid navy dot to its left while `CONCERNS`, `ABOUT`, and `BOOK CONSULTATION` remain luminous ivory white in rock-steady alignment (exact side-by-side match with `/public/assets/aistudio/image_30c907b5.png`).\n    - Scrolled past the hero and captured `.playwright-cli/nav-hover-sticky.png` while hovering `ABOUT` in the sticky alabaster header: visually verified **`\342\227\217 ABOUT`** renders cleanly with the solid `#18224B` dot and zero layout shift.\n    - Console log verified: `Total messages: 3 (Errors: 0, Warnings: 0)`.\n    - Browser closed cleanly (`Browser \'default\' closed`).\n- **What remains**:\n  - **Nothing to edit or run!** All implementation, compilation, linting, server restart, and visual hover verification for the current turn are 100% complete. Only the concise final completion response to the user remains.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Zero-layout-shift dot positioning**: Placing the `5.5px` circular dot at `absolute -left-3.5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2` inside a `relative inline-flex` button ensures neighboring navigation links never jitter horizontally when hovering any link.\n- **Crisp `#18224B` contrast on hero hover**: Removing the parent container\'s `drop-shadow` from the nav group and clearing `[text-shadow:none]` on hover keeps the hovered navy text sharp and clean over bright skin/towel hero frames, matching the user\'s reference screenshot.\n- **Existing unit test suite** (25/25 passing from prior turns; no pure-logic modules were modified in this turn).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Minor chunk match miss in `Footer.tsx`** (resolved immediately): the first `multi_replace_file_content` call updated the footer links (chunk 1) while chunk 0 missed because `Footer.tsx` imported `React` without `{ useState }`. Viewed lines 1\342\200\22312 of `Footer.tsx` and added `import { NavHoverLink } from \'./NavHoverLink\';` cleanly via `replace_file_content`. Subsequent build, lint, and browser verification all passed with 0 errors.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Dev server is running with the latest compiled build (`compile_applet` + `lint_applet` + `restart_dev_server` completed after the last edit).\n- All Playwright Chromium sessions are closed (`Browser \'default\' closed`).\n- Screenshots `.playwright-cli/nav-hover-hero.png` and `.playwright-cli/nav-hover-sticky.png` were both visually inspected and confirmed clean with zero defects.\n\n## 6. Next Steps\n1. **No further code changes or tool calls are needed.**\n2. Immediately deliver a concise, scannable, honest completion summary to the user describing:\n   - The new Odyss\303\251e-style midnight-navy `\342\227\217 LABEL` hover interaction applied across the Home Opening Horizon Navigation (`Treatments`, `Concerns`, `About`, `Book Consultation`), Sticky Header (`Menu`, `Treatments`, `Concerns`, `About`, `Book Consultation`), and Footer quick directory links\342\200\224with zero layout shift and pure `#18224B` contrast on hover.\n   - What was verified (TypeScript build & lint with zero errors, plus desktop `1440\303\227900` Chromium visual hover captures on both the Home opening hero bar and sticky header confirming the crisp midnight-navy dot/text transition and zero console errors).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Follow `ultra-mode` honest reporting (only report what was actually tested and visually inspected).\n- Keep the response concise, scannable, with no hype or raw internal file paths.\n- Never rename `metadata.json`.\n</summary>"
