    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Qualities**\n\nI\'m blown away! Those images, `about_owner_portrait_1795344836608.jpg`, `about_lounge_hero_1795344838653.jpg`, and `about_hydrangea_inset_1795344837528.jpg`, are stunning. Editorial perfection is what I\'m seeing! Museum-grade, even.\n\n\n**Matching Image Details**\n\nI\'ve been examining the image details closely. The portrait, `about_owner_portrait_1795344836608.jpg`, is an almost uncanny match to the owner\'s photo, `WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg`, with precise likeness. I\'m also seeing a perfect pairing of lounge and hydrangea images with `image_71ad232e.png`! Then, I noticed a discrepancy in the founder photo.\n\n\n**Refining Image Framing**\n\nI\'m now laser-focused on refining the framing of `about_consultation_bw_1795344839589.jpg`. I realized we can avoid a second face entirely by cropping tightly on the hands, blazer, pen, and consultation dossier. I\'m considering `object-[55%_88%] scale-[1.35]` or re-framing it to keep a focused view! Also, I think `object-cover object-[50%_75%]` or `scale-[1.45] object-[58%_85%]` would solve it. Let\'s get precise coordinates.\n\n**Adjusting Image Positioning**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the precise framing of the consultation image, realizing a specific CSS setup perfectly captures the desired elements. With `object-cover` and `origin` adjustments within an aspect ratio box, I\'m confident in achieving the sharp, monochrome view I envisioned. I\'ll verify this cropping in Chromium. Also, I\'m re-examining how Vite bundles static assets, noting a key difference between `vite dev` and `npm run build` setups.\n\n\n"
