  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Confirming Typed Imports**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed that the `tsconfig.json` setting `\"types\": [\"vite/client\"]` allows for fully native and typed ES `.jpg` imports within `.tsx` components. This works seamlessly for both development and production builds, thanks to Vite. Next, I\'m shifting my focus to carefully designing the details of the redesigned About Page (`src/components/AboutSection.tsx`).\n\n\n**Refining Visual Alignment**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in refining the visual alignment of the adaptive header, painstakingly matching its style across different scroll states of the About page, meticulously studying the provided reference screenshots. My focus now is on integrating the NOVA branding, and ensuring the Founder & Owner portrait is authentically showcased. I am going into granular detail down to typographic choices to make sure the style matches the reference!\n\n\n**Matching Visual References**\n\nI\'ve achieved pixel-perfect fidelity with `image_71ad232e.png` for the full-viewport hero section. I\'ve broken down the design into `h-screen min-h-[680px] relative w-full overflow-hidden bg-[#C7BEB5]` with the background image set up with an architectural scrim, and am working to render the header that transitions to the `#FBF9F5/95` background with midnight-navy text precisely as in the examples. Specifically, I\'m integrating the `isOverHeroMedia` prop logic I need to cleanly update `Header.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Design**\n\nI\'ve tackled the intricate details of the hero section. I\'ve ensured perfect WCAG legibility for the micro-caption, even over the sheer curtains. I\'m working on subtle GSAP scroll parallax on the hero backdrop, and am now focused on the Horizon Split Serif Headline with its dynamic positioning and typographic styling. I\'m carefully integrating the right floating still-life inset card.\n\n\n**Detailing Inset Component**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the inset component for the hero section. I\'m focusing on the rectangular frame\'s architectural edge, ensuring it matches Odyss\303\251e\'s editorial language and the `object-cover` styling of `aboutHydrangeaInsetImg`. I\'m paying close attention to the micro-caption typography and ensuring its legibility with the drop-shadow, as well as the responsive stacking for mobile. I\'m taking special care on the spacing so the hydrangea doesn\'t collide with any other text. I am also working to get the exact styling of the Philosophy Manifesto section, referencing the image.\n\n\n**Crafting Column Layout**\n\nI\'m now implementing the About page\'s core layout. I\'ve focused on the left column\'s micro-kicker, precisely styling the \"ABOUT\" text according to the specifications. I\'m now crafting the right column, placing the manifesto with the prescribed typographic details. I\'m focusing on getting the large light editorial serif manifesto to sit correctly, and I am paying attention to the indent on the text in the different viewports.\n\n\n**Implementing Contact Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the contact details for the About page, meticulously ensuring the typography and spacing align with the design specifications. I\'ve precisely styled the address and contact blocks, adhering to the specified font sizes, line heights, and colors. I am now working on ensuring proper link styling, and that everything fits as expected within the grid container.\n\nI am now focusing on the Founder & Owner Editorial Spread, replicating the exact layout and scroll motion to match the provided visual references. I will make sure the user\'s specific request for the edited owner photo is showcased in this signature moment.\n\n\n**Replicating Editorial Spread**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Founder & Owner Editorial Spread. I am focusing on making the Owner Portrait tall in the left column. I will ensure her edited portrait, with the correct aspect ratio and object position, is displayed accurately, mimicking the reference images. The flush monochrome consultation photo will be placed to its right with no gaps. I\'m focusing on perfectly rendering the photos.\n\n\n**Confirming Layout Implementation**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that a native CSS sticky layout, with `lg:sticky lg:top-[28vh]` inside an `items-stretch` grid column, works perfectly for the editorial spread! I\'ve confirmed that this layout renders fluidly and performantly with no `overflow-hidden` constraints. The monochrome consultation photo will be placed flush adjacent, with the correct frame and styling. I am now working on the responsive implementation with the correct styling and `object-cover grayscale`.\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Composition**\n\nI\'m now carefully implementing the rightmost column\'s whitespace, ensuring the serene aesthetic aligns with the references. The hands-and-dossier photo is being placed at the appropriate scale and position to preserve its intended effect. I will add the founder attribution, including the kicker, heading, and bio, and a clean action link. I am making sure the founder is properly recognized.\n\n\n**Implementing Sanctuary Pillars**\n\nI\'m now implementing the three-column sanctuary notes band, focusing on the refined hairline division and the presentation of NOVA\'s pillars: Private Suites, Considered Formulations, and Unhurried Scheduling. I am ensuring the Explore Treatments and Book Consultation links trigger the correct transitions. I\'ve removed the (Placeholder) staff bios, and I am focused on keeping the About page cohesive with the aesthetic.\n\n\n"
