  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Imperfections**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the inspection! Those four captures are near-luxury editorial quality already. Visually, we caught three crystal-clear defects and uncovered a unit test regression. The Senior Product Designer\'s critique, identifying the top four defects (starting with the most severe), is invaluable. I\'m focusing on those findings.\n\n\n**Addressing Clipping Issue**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the clipping issue! Comparing `about-r1-hero.png` and `image_71ad232e.png` reveals the discrepancy. The large dimensions and positioning cause the inset card\'s caption to be clipped at the bottom. My immediate focus is on a concrete fix: adjusting the `lg` and `xl` styles to properly position and scale the hydrangea card. I\'m aiming for it to match the reference image and avoid any caption clipping. This involves adjusting the top position, width, and aspect ratio.\n\n\n**Refining Composition Focus**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the monochrome photo framing. The current cropping cuts across the chins, and I need a fix. I\'m adjusting the zoom and anchor to focus precisely on the hands, blazer, pen, dossier, and table, matching the reference image. The goal is to eliminate any chin cut-off by using a scale and object that fits the editorial composition. The final zoom will be to `scale-[1.92] object-[54%_95%] origin-[56%_88%]`.\n\n\n"
