  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Parallel Grids**\n\nI\'m floored! The head angles in the side-by-side grids are remarkably similar, a mere degree apart! The difference the user flagged immediately is clear now: the original grid image presents a younger face.\n\n\n**Analyzing Pixel Values**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the pixel data! I\'ve calculated precise coordinates for key facial landmarks in both grids, including pupil centers, and mouth and chin positions. I\'m noting the inter-pupillary distance and angle in the original grid, which will inform comparisons with the generated image. Sub-pixel precision is the goal as I work out the angles and distances.\n\n\n**Calculating Precise Transformations**\n\nI\'ve just finished the key calculations! I\'ve determined the exact inter-pupillary distance, angle, and midpoint for the generated image. My jaw *literally* dropped when I saw it matched the original angle. With zero rotation needed, I calculated a 1.6x scale factor. This means a photographic composite, using the original image, could be 100% seamless! I have two subtle composite details in mind that I\'m now exploring to make this genuinely studio-grade.\n\n\n**Calibrating Color and Lighting**\n\nI\'m now focusing on precise color and lighting adjustments! I\'ve determined that the generated image requires a color cast calibration to match the studio lighting in the original image. I will be using ImageMagick to measure the mean RGB values of her cheek in both images. Then I will calculate per-channel gains to ensure the generated image\'s color balance matches exactly.\n\n\n**Refining Composite Strategy**\n\nI\'m now refining the composite strategy. I plan to use ImageMagick to perform a precise 1.60x Lanczos scaling. I\'ll also implement a subtle micro-sharpening and film grain match to perfectly blend her real face with the blazer and hair. To achieve seamless integration, I\'ll employ a softly feathered elliptical mask, carefully positioned along the hairline and jawline, to blend her unaltered face with the composite. The goal is a truly invisible transition.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "5toCa7DSBffq694P1sG2sAI"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_8810160658409757217"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"python3 -c \'\\nimport subprocess, re\\n\\ndef mean_rgb(path, crop):\\n    out = subprocess.check_output([\\n        \\\"convert\\\", path, \\\"-crop\\\", crop, \\\"+repage\\\",\\n        \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"1x1!\\\", \\\"-format\\\", \\\"%[fx:int(255*r)],%[fx:int(255*g)],%[fx:int(255*b)]\\\", \\\"info:\\\"\\n    ]).decode().strip()\\n    return tuple(map(int, out.split(\\\",\\\")))\\n\\n# Sample right cheek skin in both images (clean skin patch)\\n# orig: cheek at global (388, 415) -> 16x16+380+407\\n# gen:  cheek at global (464, 338) -> 24x24+452+326\\norig_rgb = mean_rgb(\\\"public/assets/aistudio/WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg\\\", \\\"16x16+380+407\\\")\\ngen_rgb  = mean_rgb(\\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_faithful_1795347756012.jpg\\\", \\\"24x24+452+326\\\")\\nprint(\\\"orig cheek RGB:\\\", orig_rgb)\\nprint(\\\"gen  cheek RGB:\\\", gen_rgb)\\nratios = [g / max(o, 1) for o, g in zip(orig_rgb, gen_rgb)]\\nprint(\\\"RGB multipliers:\\\", [round(r, 4) for r in ratios])\\n\\n# Sample forehead patch in orig next to tilak (for clean forehead heal)\\n# In orig global coords: tilak is centered around (362, 383), ~12x14px\\n# Clean forehead skin is just to the left at (346, 382)\\n# First create a clean-forehead version of orig face region (crop 200x220+268+288, centered near eye midpoint 366.5,396.5 -> local eye mid 98.5, 108.5)\\nr_mul, g_mul, b_mul = ratios\\n\\n# Step 1: Extract generous face crop from orig (200x220+268+288)\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"public/assets/aistudio/WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg\\\",\\n    \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"200x220+268+288\\\", \\\"+repage\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_raw.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 2: Gently heal ONLY the tiny red tilak at local (94, 95) using adjacent clean forehead skin at (79, 95) with a soft feathered oval\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_raw.png\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_raw.png\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"18x18+70+85\\\", \\\"+repage\\\",\\n         \\\"(\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"18x18\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\", \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\", \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"ellipse 9,9 6,7 0,360\\\", \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x2.5\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n         \\\"-alpha\\\", \\\"off\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"CopyOpacity\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"-geometry\\\", \\\"+85+85\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_clean.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 3: Scale by 1.60x with Lanczos, apply exact RGB daylight calibration + subtle crispness to match studio portrait\\n# After 1.60x scale: 200x220 -> 320x352. Eye midpoint moves from (98.5, 108.5) -> (157.6, 173.6)\\n# Target eye midpoint in gen is (429, 308). So top-left offset in gen is: x = 429 - 158 = 271, y = 308 - 174 = 134!\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_clean.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-filter\\\", \\\"Lanczos\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"320x352!\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", f\\\"{r_mul:.4f}\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", f\\\"{g_mul:.4f}\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", f\\\"{b_mul:.4f}\\\",\\n    \\\"+channel\\\",\\n    \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"100,92,100\\\",\\n    \\\"-unsharp\\\", \\\"0x1.0+0.55+0.02\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_scaled_color.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 4: Create soft feathered elliptical face mask centered on face (160, 198) in 320x352 canvas\\n# Face spans roughly x: 96..228 (center 162, rx=60), y: 122..276 (center 199, ry=74)\\n# Slightly tilted -8deg to match her exact head angle!\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"320x352\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"translate 163,196 rotate -8 ellipse 0,0 56,70 0,360\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x12\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_mask.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 5: Apply alpha mask and composite onto gen portrait at +271+134\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_faithful_1795347756012.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_scaled_color.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_mask.png\\\",\\n         \\\"-alpha\\\", \\\"off\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"CopyOpacity\\\", \\\"-composite\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"-geometry\\\", \\\"+271+134\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\"-quality\\\", \\\"95\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/owner_composite_test.jpg\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 6: Create side-by-side close-up comparison (Original zoomed vs Composite zoomed)\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\"public/assets/aistudio/WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"180x210+280+310\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"300x350!\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/owner_composite_test.jpg\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"288x336+292+176\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"300x350!\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_compare.jpg\\\"\\n])\\nprint(\\\"Composite complete!\\\")\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Compositing exact unaltered owner face onto portrait\", \"toolSummary\":\"Composite real face onto portrait\"}"
