    thinking: "**Analyzing Perfect Skin Tone**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed! The skin tone match in `owner_portrait_real_face.jpg` is phenomenal. The transition from neck to face, cheeks, eyes, nose, lips and expression are indistinguishable from her real photo. It\'s almost perfect; one tiny detail needs addressing.\n\n\n**Refining The Forehead Solution**\n\nI\'ve hit on a breakthrough! Instead of patching the forehead with guesswork, I realized I can directly use the pristine forehead skin from `owner_portrait_faithful_1795347756012.jpg`! My plan is to create a feathered mask that cleanly covers everything *except* the forehead and tilak. This preserves the original features perfectly and seamlessly integrates the clean forehead skin. The soft feathering will blend the transition. It\'s a much smarter approach!\n\n\n"
