  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining a Recent Idea**\n\nI realized the user\'s comment arrived *right* after saving the `owner_portrait_final_exact.jpg` file and updating `AboutSection.tsx`. It\'s clear that we can improve the result before even compiling! I\'m thinking how to make it **EVEN BETTER** before compiling and restarting the system.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Final Image**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into `owner_portrait_final_exact.jpg` to identify the slight softness around the eyes and nostrils. I\'ve pinpointed an overlap issue with the mask and the under-chin shadow and hair edge. The upscaling from a medium-distance photo contributes to this, alongside a subtle violet tint from the gamma settings. I\'m focusing on achieving flawless geometry and studio-level clarity by removing that violet tint.\n\n\n**Optimizing Color & Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on neutralizing the orange tones in the image. I plan to use a warm-to-cool LAB/HSL white-balance shift to refine the color. My goal is to maintain the clarity of her eyes and eyebrows by using an edge-aware clarity approach, which will avoid the previous violet cast. I am now avoiding any change to the real face pixels! I am looking into her cheek RGB, the original vs the target to analyze the original image\'s color composition.\n\n\n**Implementing the Image Fix**\n\nI\'m now implementing the white-balance fix using ImageMagick `-modulate`. I\'m fine-tuning the hue rotation to subtly shift the orange-red tones toward a golden-warm beige. My focus is on avoiding any violet/magenta cast in the eyes or lips. I\'m also incorporating a subtle neutral contrast adjustment and a tighter inner-face mask to preserve the hair edge and studio jawline, while precisely positioning her facial features. I\'m also adding a subtle warm-neutral lighting gradient to match the soft window falloff.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "AuYCa_icJabaqtsPt5-qwQo"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11871638968283164812"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"python3 -c \'\\nimport subprocess\\n\\n# Step 1: Extract raw unmodified face crop from original photo (200x220+268+288)\\n# Apply gentle photographic white-balance (NO harsh blue gamma that creates purple eye/nostril tints!)\\n# Shift hue slightly warmer-golden (+2.2 in ImageMagick 0..200 scale where 100 is neutral), reduce orange saturation to 82%,\\n# gently tame R highlight and lift B only slightly (1.06) so whites of eyes stay pure white and blacks stay pure black!\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"public/assets/aistudio/WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg\\\",\\n    \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"200x220+268+288\\\", \\\"+repage\\\",\\n    \\\"-filter\\\", \\\"Lanczos\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"320x352!\\\",\\n    \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"96,80,102.4\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.86\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", \\\"0.94\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.98\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", \\\"1.00\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.08\\\", \\\"-evaluate\\\", \\\"multiply\\\", \\\"1.04\\\",\\n    \\\"+channel\\\",\\n    \\\"-sigmoidal-contrast\\\", \\\"2.2,52%\\\",\\n    \\\"-attenuate\\\", \\\"0.08\\\", \\\"+noise\\\", \\\"Gaussian\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_color6.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\nrgb_check = subprocess.check_output([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_color6.png\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"24x24+182+190\\\", \\\"+repage\\\",\\n    \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"1x1!\\\", \\\"-format\\\", \\\"%[fx:int(255*r)],%[fx:int(255*g)],%[fx:int(255*b)]\\\", \\\"info:\\\"\\n]).decode().strip()\\nprint(\\\"v6 calibrated cheek RGB:\\\", rgb_check, \\\"(target gen cheek: 203,151,125)\\\")\\n\\n# Step 2: Build precision feathered face mask that keeps 100% of her real eyes, brows, nose, cheeks, lips, and chin\\n# while smoothly feathering into the studio hairline & jaw shadow AND cleanly letting studio forehead skin cover the tiny tilak\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"320x352\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"translate 162,197 rotate -8 ellipse 0,0 53,68 0,360\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x10\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"320x352\\\", \\\"xc:white\\\",\\n         \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"black\\\",\\n         \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"ellipse 150,146 13,15 0,360\\\",\\n         \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x6\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Multiply\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_mask6.png\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 3: Composite cleanly onto studio editorial portrait\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_faithful_1795347756012.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_color6.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_mask6.png\\\",\\n         \\\"-alpha\\\", \\\"off\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"CopyOpacity\\\", \\\"-composite\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"-geometry\\\", \\\"+271+134\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\"-quality\\\", \\\"95\\\",\\n    \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_studio_real.jpg\\\"\\n])\\n\\n# Step 4: Side-by-side close-up comparison\\nsubprocess.check_call([\\n    \\\"convert\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\"public/assets/aistudio/WhatsApp_Image_2026-11-22_at_14.49.44_890263a1.jpeg\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"180x210+280+310\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"300x350!\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_studio_real.jpg\\\", \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"288x336+292+176\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"300x350!\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_compare_v6.jpg\\\"\\n])\\nprint(\\\"v6 complete!\\\")\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Refining neutral daylight balance on real owner face\", \"toolSummary\":\"Refine real-face lighting balance\"}"
