  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Subtle Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the outer cheek regions in `neck_zoom_check2.png`. I noticed something interesting! Specifically, the edges of both cheeks, near the dark hair on each side, seem to hold a crucial clue. It\'s a subtle detail, but I\'m confident that it warrants further inspection.\n\n\n**Analyzing Cheek Details**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! I can see a pale skin halo, or faint double-line, on the viewer\'s left outer cheek. It\'s a 3-5px effect, likely due to the polygon hugging the dark hair boundary. On the right side, there\'s a pinkish blush strip and a soft dark vertical seam at the cheek transition. I\'m excited about how surgically clean this is, as it allows for fixing both outer cheeks without impacting the rest of the face!\n\n\n**Refining Cheek Edges**\n\nI\'ve got it! Extending the left polygon edge just 5px into her actual dark hair fully eliminates the pale outer skin ridge and any seams on the left cheek. That dark glossy hair from `grid_orig.png` is the solution. The right cheek\'s rosy blush is a bit brighter, but it still blends with the daylight shadow.\n\n\n"
