  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Image Refinement**\n\nI\'m amazed! The refinement in `cheek_zoom_check.png` is striking. The image has vastly improved, and I\'ve honed in on the sole remaining issue: a tiny, 4px crescent sliver on the bottom-left outer cheek, specifically at x=80-95 and y=135-148. This is the last hurdle.\n\n\n**Analyzing Cheek Boundary Detail**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the persistence of that stubborn sliver. It seems the original polygon edge at (88, 142) was *too* close to the base image\'s broader cheek, extending out by 4px! Comparing `grid_gen.png` and `grid_orig.png`, the polygon was too conservative. By extending the two lower-left polygon points a mere 10px further down-left, the issue should vanish. Examining base files, I\'m confident in this proposed adjustment.\n\n\n"
