  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Jawline Improvement**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the jawline progress! Comparing the \'before\' and \'after\' in `jaw_before_after.png`, specifically the right panel, is eye-opening. The left lower cheek/jaw (`viewer-left`) looks significantly cleaner now, with a crisp, natural jawline and no bluish tint! This is excellent.\n\n\n**Refining Facial Details**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough with the facial details! I realized I miscalculated the tilak\'s location, fixing this by retaining the upper face from `v2_394.png` since it\'s already perfect. Now, I\'m intensely focusing on refining the jawline. Specifically, I see a small imperfection on both sides, near the jaw, between the earlobe and jawline curve, which need attention and careful refinement from `v2_394.png`.\n\n\n**Observing Jawline Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the jawline features. Focusing on the right panel\'s lower-right cheek reveals it\'s warmer and smoother, which is exciting. However, there\'s a tiny faint bump at the outer edge, which I must address. Also, I\'m noting the lower-left jaw\'s clean, soft light edge. Importantly, the rest of the face is already ideal.\n\n\n**Perfecting Jawline Edges**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on those two specific areas. For the lower-left edge, I\'m integrating warm studio hair from `about_owner_portrait_1795344836608.jpg` to eliminate the bluish patch and refine the double-edge along the jaw. I\'m using a crisp 2.2px feather, with her crisp real lower-left cheek from `face_clean_jaw.png` inside, for a seamless blend. The right side requires further attention.\n\n\n**Detailing Right Jawline**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the right jawline. Using a surgical patch approach, I\'m examining specific pixel ranges to understand the interplay of shadow and skin. The grey shadow in `v2_394.png` seems to be a combination of a darkened edge and the base image\'s hair shadow. My strategy involves integrating the clean, warm cheek from `face_clean_jaw.png` with studio hair from `about_owner_portrait_1795344836608.jpg` to craft a natural jawline curve.\n\n\n"
