  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Pixel Data**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! Examining `jaw_tight_compare.png` at 3x zoom is paying off. The left side (lower cheek/jaw in the right panel) appears fully contracted. This is critical for assessing the asymmetry. I\'m focusing on the pixel-level detail for definitive evidence.\n\n\n**Refining Asymmetry Analysis**\n\nI\'ve got it! The bluish hair spot and double edge are gone; the jaw curves naturally now. The right side shows two key issues: `right_hair_bg_mask` went too far down and covered part of the lapel. The left panel shows a pale-greyish/greenish-tinted skin strip and a tiny diagonal seam on the cheek. I\'m addressing these issues.\n\n\n**Identifying Color Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial observation. Analyzing the images, particularly `exact2_scaled.png`, I realized the grayish outer cheek edge near the ear is a result of desaturating skin, turning warm peach to grayish-beige where a specular/flash bounce and hair shadow existed. The left cheek also highlights the success in eliminating the bluish-purple hair spot. This is key to addressing the color discrepancies effectively.\n\n\n**Perfecting Jaw Tone**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on the right side now. It\'s crucial to leave the neck and lapel alone; they are pristine. My focus is on replacing the ashy lower cheek zone with her natural, warm skin tone from `face_v2tone.png`, maintaining full saturation and adjusting the hue. I\'ll softly blend the hair/ear border to create a seamless transition. The goal is a warm, golden-peach cheek that matches flawlessly, eliminating any grey patches or pink rims.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "xw8Da6GPM7OIqtsPrtf2oQM"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_12174105000983468057"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"python3 -c \'\\nimport subprocess\\n\\n# 1. Start from v2_394.png (perfect forehead, eyes, nose, lips, chin, neck, blazer collar)\\n# Apply ONLY the proven flawless LEFT lower-jaw hair backdrop patch (eliminates bluish hair + left outer jaw halo)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/v2_394.png\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/base_394.png\\\", \\\"-roll\\\", \\\"+18+4\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/left_hair_bg_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/v3_left_bg.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 2. Build the warm, healthy skin-tone real cheek layer from exact2_scaled.png\\n#    Match her exact warm golden-peach skin tone (NO grey desaturation!)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/exact2_scaled.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"98,86,102.0\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.99\\\",\\n    \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.015\\\",\\n    \\\"+channel\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_warm_skin.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# On ONLY the right outer cheekbone blush area (x=230..258, y=155..222), shift pink -> warm golden-peach\\n# (keep saturation ~92% so it NEVER looks grey/ashy, just slightly warmer hue + subtle red-channel calm)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"394x394\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 228,150 260,150 258,225 228,228 234,188\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x9\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/r_warm_blush_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_warm_skin.png\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/face_warm_skin.png\\\",\\n         \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"98,92,104.2\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.965\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.01\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.975\\\",\\n         \\\"+channel\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/r_warm_blush_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_warm_clean.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 3. Mask ONLY the lower-left and lower-right cheek/jaw zones:\\n#    - Left lower cheek/jaw: crisp 2.2px feather along exact real left jaw contour\\n#    - Right lower cheek/jaw: warm real cheek all the way out to x=251 (right up to the ear/hair edge)\\n#      and curving cleanly down the right jaw (246,214 -> 236,230 -> 220,242), STOPPING cleanly above the neck/collar!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"394x394\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    # Left lower cheek/jaw\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 125,180 158,184 166,238 164,244 150,235 138,222 130,204\\\",\\n    # Right lower cheek/jaw (hugging natural contour cleanly into earlobe & jaw-to-neck curve)\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 220,164 252,166 253,188 250,206 244,221 234,234 218,244 206,244 210,222 216,192\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x2.6\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/both_jaw_sides_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/v3_left_bg.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/face_warm_clean.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/both_jaw_sides_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/merged_jaw_v3.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 4. Also warm-harmonize the tiny 4px skin/hair transition strip right in front of the earlobe (x=245..256, y=184..216)\\n#    using a subtle warm skin glaze so no cool grey pixel remains at the ear/cheek junction\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"394x394\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 243,178 255,180 253,212 243,225 239,220 245,200\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x4\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/r_ear_junction_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/merged_jaw_v3.png\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/merged_jaw_v3.png\\\",\\n         \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"97,108,101.5\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.94\\\",\\n         \\\"+channel\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/r_ear_junction_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/merged_jaw_v3_final.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# Place back onto the full 848x1264 v2 image\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_clean_cheeks_v2.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/merged_jaw_v3_final.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/box_mask.png\\\", \\\"-alpha\\\", \\\"off\\\", \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"CopyOpacity\\\", \\\"-composite\\\", \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\"-geometry\\\", \\\"+254+166\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\"-quality\\\", \\\"95\\\",\\n    \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_clean_jaw.jpg\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# Create before/after closeups (normal + 3x tight jaw zoom)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_clean_jaw.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"320x320+260+180\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"640x640\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_inspect_after3.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_inspect_before.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_inspect_after3.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_before_after3.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_clean_jaw.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"220x130+340+320\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"660x390\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_tight_after3.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_tight_before.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_tight_after3.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/jaw_tight_compare3.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nprint(\\\"Done v3\\\")\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\".\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Applying warm skin-tone jaw cleanup\", \"toolSummary\":\"Apply warm jaw cleanup\"}"
