  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Data**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the visual data, specifically `tone_check_before.png`. Focusing on the chest/collarbone, hand, face, and upper neck, I\'m noting distinct color tones. The chest and hand exhibit a cool-neutral editorial studio daylight tone, while the face and upper neck seem distinct. I\'m noting the RGB values to quantify these observations.\n\n\n**Matching Color Tones Precisely**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on precise color matching between the face/upper neck and the chest/lower neck.  My focus is on achieving an RGB value of approximately `205, 155, 127` on the face, to align with the chest. I\'m carefully calibrating a channel lift/gamma process with gentle desaturation, specifically targeting the face and upper neck skin. I need to preserve the darkness of her eyes, brows, lashes, etc., while subtly warming the facial tones.\n\n\n**Calculating Gamma Corrections**\n\nI\'ve determined the exact gamma values required for each color channel. Red needs a gentle gamma of approximately 0.96. Green requires a gamma of around 1.175 to lift midtones smoothly while preserving black details. Blue necessitates a gamma of roughly 1.34. To ensure deep blacks in pupils, brows, and lashes without unwanted blue shadows, I\'m considering luminance-weighted skin masks or black-point anchoring on the Blue channel, perhaps even a skin-only luminance mask combined with a spatial mask for precise targeting.\n\n\n**Refining Luminance Masking**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the luminance-gated skin mask approach. Multiplying a face/upper-neck spatial mask with a soft luminance gate (black pixels < 22%, skin pixels > 42%) cleanly shifts skin from golden-orange to creamy, matching the chest and hand. This leaves eyebrows, eyelashes, pupils, and dark hair untouched, preserving eye sharpness. Lips retain their rosy warmth, too. I\'m excited to refine this with a unified editorial finish.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "kBgDa_34O5rPnsEPw_mqsA4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14744157202518228816"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"python3 -c \'\\nimport subprocess\\n\\nsrc = \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_clean_jaw.jpg\\\"\\n\\n# 1. Build spatial mask covering the face + upper neck (the warmer tungsten-cast region)\\n#    Coordinates in full 848x1264 image (offset +254+166):\\n#    Face center ~(438, 345), upper neck ~(445, 435), tapering smoothly down to lower neck ~(445, 480)\\n#    where skin already matches the chest!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"848x1264\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    # Face + upper neck polygon (generous around face because luminance mask protects hair/brows/eyes!)\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 365,245 440,225 515,260 525,355 505,435 495,485 385,485 375,420 355,340\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x24\\\",\\n    # Lightly attenuate right over the lips (around 438,376) so lips retain natural rosy warmth\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"gray45\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"ellipse 438,376 26,11 0,360\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x5\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_spatial_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 2. Build luminance gate from the source image so dark eyes, eyebrows, lashes, nostrils, and dark hair\\n#    are 100% protected from Blue/Green midtone lift!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", src,\\n    \\\"-colorspace\\\", \\\"Gray\\\",\\n    \\\"-level\\\", \\\"24%,54%\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x2\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_lum_gate.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# Combine spatial mask * luminance gate -> precision skin-only mask!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_spatial_mask.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_lum_gate.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Multiply\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_skin_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 3. Create the studio-daylight skin-matched version of the image:\\n#    Current cheek: (206, 142, 101) -> Target (lower neck / chest): (204, 156, 129)\\n#    R gamma=0.96, G gamma=1.15, B gamma=1.32 brings (206,142,101) -> ~(204,155,127)\\n#    Also slightly calm forehead excess brightness if needed? Forehead is 208,165,137 (already close to 205,156,129!)\\n#    Wait: forehead (y=250..295) is ALREADY 208,165,137 \342\200\224 let us keep forehead at ~35% strength so forehead\\n#    does not get over-cooled while cheeks, chin, and upper neck (y=305..475) get 100% match!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"848x1264\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    # Full strength on cheeks, nose, chin, upper neck (y=302..472)\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 365,302 520,300 518,415 500,478 385,478 375,415 358,350\\\",\\n    # Gentle 40% blend on forehead (already close to body tone!)\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"gray40\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 378,242 440,228 508,258 518,302 365,302\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x18\\\",\\n    # Protect natural rosy lips (keep 60% original lip rose)\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"gray40\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"ellipse 438,376 26,11 0,360\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x5\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_spatial_mask2.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_spatial_mask2.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_lum_gate.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Multiply\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_skin_mask2.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", src,\\n    \\\"(\\\", src,\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"0.96\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.14\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.30\\\",\\n         \\\"+channel\\\",\\n         \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"101,94,100\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_skin_mask2.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\"-quality\\\", \\\"95\\\",\\n    \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_matched_tone.jpg\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 4. Verify resulting RGB skin tones across the entire body!\\ndef avg_rgb(img, geom):\\n    return subprocess.check_output([\\n        \\\"convert\\\", img, \\\"-crop\\\", geom, \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"1x1!\\\",\\n        \\\"-format\\\", \\\"%[fx:int(255*r)],%[fx:int(255*g)],%[fx:int(255*b)] (lum=%[fx:int(255*(0.299*r+0.587*g+0.114*b))])\\\", \\\"info:\\\"\\n    ]).decode().strip()\\n\\nout = \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_matched_tone.jpg\\\"\\nzones = [\\n    (\\\"Forehead\\\",      \\\"30x20+415+275\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Mid-left chk\\\",  \\\"24x24+395+338\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Mid-right chk\\\", \\\"24x24+468+332\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Chin\\\",          \\\"24x16+428+395\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Upper neck\\\",    \\\"34x22+430+430\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Lower neck\\\",    \\\"40x30+425+485\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Chest/decoll\\\",  \\\"44x34+415+535\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Hand/knuckles\\\", \\\"36x28+372+868\\\"),\\n]\\nprint(\\\"=== AFTER TONE MATCH ===\\\")\\nfor name, geom in zones:\\n    print(f\\\"{name:15s}: {avg_rgb(out, geom)}\\\")\\n\\n# Create side-by-side comparison (face + torso + hand)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", out, \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"480x760+185+170\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"480x760\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_check_after.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_check_before.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/tone_check_after.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/tone_before_after.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\".\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Matching face and neck tone to body daylight tone\", \"toolSummary\":\"Match face tone to body\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\343%\n\340%\001i\024}\023\272\204e\210\351\302Iy\017\3434j\001\237v\\\363\204\313\327@T\203S\001\217\217\330p\035\034Aqb\367\205\223;\250T\3514nO\247L\225\031\215\271cN\234\262\212\n\355Y\312\350F>\207\3123\264\370\177\305\230\344\3258.\263\222\334\3656\327\312\316\230\377\214\335\241^\036\033\211\217\274_m\310H\374\334\206>&4\353\324\211\213\370\"C\361\232\024)\321\236NC)\332\306=]3\257*\220\357\326\331\026\251\305-\202$y\270~O]s\353\264\2246\232\270\343\022Hz6\305\371\000\273\177\005\334;^51\361u\236r}\227@ST\3548A\377\335\366W\256\025\234\276\321\247\251\305\357\345&\314(\242\254X,\236<\002\303\276\\sn\214\211\364\341h+b\333c\357\a\222\235\000\213\352\340\373\260\236E\345P\240\304\245\202\235\243\270\346\274\231l\245T\025\363\037~\271\320-\024N.\345\232\210\214j\371\'\020u\242\243\241\260\317\273\335\266\325\036\213H,\251\273\310,\222\326HH\334F\021 \300\213\034\027\377P\342\r!ZK\003p\357\222\307\310v\204]]\347\335B\255E\212\371\211\026\313\035\353P\325?\037x\352b\216\362\002\252\323\021/a\270tFd\215\b\231\351\2178\354\341\243\345g\302\004\321\235\367\211\326\312vU\243\207\244\aE\330<\230\265\353_\312\221|N\224\300\033\241tl\f\340\022\022\237\003\033\000\331\023\223\263p-\004\251\222\337\b\312\312\006\341w\300.\345q\257\270ueG\272Jd\375\rYD\017\333\274\303\216}\227\'2@S\247;\a_\300t^LV\216M\001em\207L\255\026\203\023%}\205<\203\017\307\325\351Z\217v~\036RgnL\233d=\033\346B7\241\306}\225)\240\230\030\343\275M\217\324\3226\354\036s6\364\364\364p\272s{\034u(\311\0009\376\326\225\f\327$\352\252\262\033\027\304\003\256\000*e\363:\226\341gg\021\317\234\236\026\240\v\2768\326\\\223y\023\357\037\017\376\v\005\023;\232\331.#o\372\363\310`\022\221;E\316\311\241\267\037\031\020:&\034\276\227q[\242a\377L\177\335\346\324\327\177\352m\300\214o\342V}\273\225\321\302\253N\341\337\373c\351\346\214\315\304\364\336\247\261]c\032\307\260\024\v\254\327-\005\316>\334\275io]8Z\311\aB8\223\b\327Bh\036D\246\023\220\r\343\r\334\256\305@y\233\265 \306T}CR\02