  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Clarity Emerge**\n\nI\'m struck by the precision now. Each exposed skin area is laid bare, mapped with perfect pixel coordinates from the established grid\'s origin at x=170, y=380, and squares measuring 25px. The initial focus is on the neck, collarbone and chest area, specifically where a V-neck would sit.\n\n\n**Defining Skin & Garment**\n\nI\'ve established pixel coordinates for key areas, including the neck and collar. The collar\'s edges are defined by several coordinates, and I\'ve focused on using a skin chroma check to distinguish skin from fabric, ensuring no cloth is included. I\'ve also begun mapping the wrist, hand, and fingers, noting the color contrast.\n\n\n**Refining Masking Approach**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into refining the chroma-gated skin mask. The back of the hand and fingers are mapped, and I\'ve identified the rectangular watch with its distinct dark brown leather strap and bright watch face. The crucial breakthrough is the skin-hue and saturation mask, which perfectly isolates the hand/wrist pixels while ignoring the clothing and watch components. I\'m incredibly excited because of how clean the mask is for both the neck/chest and hand/wrist areas.\n\n\n**Isolating Skin Pixels**\n\nI\'ve crafted an ImageMagick-based skin mask that\'s incredibly precise. Within the defined polygons for the neck, chest, hand, and wrist, I\'m using color comparisons to isolate skin. The key is analyzing `r - b` values, along with a check on the red channel, which produces a mask that precisely follows all of the skin edges, which is really clean! I am now working on adjusting the skin luminance to match the subject\'s face using an empirical model of luminance values.\n\n\n**Adjusting Luminance Levels**\n\nI\'m now focusing on luminance adjustments. I plan to boost the neck and chest by +1 to +1.5 shades, slightly cooler. My goal is for these areas to sit around `lum ~174-182`, matching her luminous face. The hand and wrist require a more significant ~2-shade lift, using a warmer daylight balance to take them from the current darker tones to a `lum ~145`, which I think is much better.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "aR0Da8jJGua5sOIPmeWjsA8"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_15110869816541347984"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"python3 -c \'\\nimport subprocess\\n\\nsrc = \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_matched_tone.jpg\\\"\\n\\n# 1. Build automatic sub-pixel skin chroma gate across the whole image using -fx:\\n#    Skin has r > g > b, warm chroma (r - b) > 0.08, and r > 0.24 (excludes navy trousers where b>r,\\n#    excludes ivory blazer/camisole/watch dial where r-b < 0.07, excludes black hair/piping/watch strap where r < 0.24)\\n#    Use smooth ramps so edges around fingers, collar, silk V-neck, and watch strap are silky-smooth!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", src,\\n    \\\"-fx\\\", \\\"clamp((r - b - 0.065)*10, 0, 1) * clamp((r - g - 0.025)*14, 0, 1) * clamp((r - 0.22)*8, 0, 1) * clamp((0.92 - b)*8, 0, 1)\\\",\\n    \\\"-colorspace\\\", \\\"Gray\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x1.2\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/skin_chroma_gate.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 2. Spatial mask A: Neck & Chest/Collarbone (everything from right under chin down to silk V-neck)\\n#    Start smoothly right at the bottom of the jawline (y=412) so chin-to-neck transition stays 100% seamless!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"848x1264\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 380,415 516,408 518,460 470,582 378,582 376,470\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x12\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/neck_chest_region.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/neck_chest_region.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/skin_chroma_gate.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Multiply\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/neck_chest_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 3. Spatial mask B: Wrist, Hand, & Fingers (resting on navy trousers)\\n#    Also explicitly exclude the watch face/bezel area with a soft dark ellipse just in case gold/rose bezel has warm chroma!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"-size\\\", \\\"848x1264\\\", \\\"xc:black\\\",\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"white\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 325,905 385,855 475,800 538,838 518,895 452,955 340,965 322,938\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x6\\\",\\n    # Protect watch dial & leather strap around (475,862) rotated ~-42 deg\\n    \\\"-fill\\\", \\\"black\\\",\\n    \\\"-draw\\\", \\\"polygon 452,844 472,832 498,874 478,888\\\",\\n    \\\"-blur\\\", \\\"0x2\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/hand_wrist_region.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/hand_wrist_region.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/skin_chroma_gate.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Multiply\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/hand_wrist_mask.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 4. Lighten Neck & Chest by ~1.5 shades (creamy daylight match to her luminous face!)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", src,\\n    \\\"(\\\", src,\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.14\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.18\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.21\\\",\\n         \\\"+channel\\\",\\n         \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"103,95,100\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/neck_chest_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/body_step1_neck.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# 5. Lighten Hand, Fingers, & Wrist by ~2 shades (lifting deep lap-shadow brown up to matching fair creamy daylight tone!)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_step1_neck.png\\\",\\n    \\\"(\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_step1_neck.png\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"R\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.34\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"G\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.42\\\",\\n         \\\"-channel\\\", \\\"B\\\", \\\"-gamma\\\", \\\"1.45\\\",\\n         \\\"+channel\\\",\\n         \\\"-modulate\\\", \\\"106,90,100.5\\\",\\n    \\\")\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/hand_wrist_mask.png\\\",\\n    \\\"-compose\\\", \\\"Over\\\", \\\"-composite\\\",\\n    \\\"-quality\\\", \\\"95\\\",\\n    \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_light_body.jpg\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# Check RGB values across the entire body!\\ndef avg_rgb(img, geom):\\n    return subprocess.check_output([\\n        \\\"convert\\\", img, \\\"-crop\\\", geom, \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"1x1!\\\",\\n        \\\"-format\\\", \\\"%[fx:int(255*r)],%[fx:int(255*g)],%[fx:int(255*b)] (lum=%[fx:int(255*(0.299*r+0.587*g+0.114*b))])\\\", \\\"info:\\\"\\n    ]).decode().strip()\\n\\nout = \\\"src/assets/images/owner_portrait_light_body.jpg\\\"\\nfor name, geom in [\\n    (\\\"Forehead\\\",      \\\"30x20+415+275\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Mid-left chk\\\",  \\\"24x24+395+338\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Mid-right chk\\\", \\\"24x24+468+332\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Upper neck\\\",    \\\"34x22+430+430\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Lower neck\\\",    \\\"40x30+425+485\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Chest/decoll\\\",  \\\"44x34+415+535\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Wrist\\\",         \\\"28x24+486+838\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Hand/back\\\",     \\\"36x28+412+885\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Fingers\\\",       \\\"32x24+372+912\\\"),\\n]:\\n    print(f\\\"{name:15s}: {avg_rgb(out, geom)}\\\")\\n\\n# Create side-by-side full portrait comparison (before vs after)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", src, \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"520x820+165+175\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_before.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", out, \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"520x820+165+175\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_after.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", \\\"+append\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_before.png\\\", \\\".playwright-cli/body_after.png\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/body_before_after.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\\n# Also inspect tight closeup of the hand + watch to verify zero bleed onto trousers/watch/cuff!\\nsubprocess.run([\\n    \\\"convert\\\", out, \\\"-crop\\\", \\\"260x220+315+790\\\", \\\"+repage\\\", \\\"-resize\\\", \\\"520x440\\\",\\n    \\\".playwright-cli/hand_closeup_check.png\\\"\\n], check=True)\\n\'\", \"Cwd\":\".\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000, \"toolAction\":\"Lightening neck, chest, wrist, and hand skin to match face tone\", \"toolSummary\":\"Lighten body skin to match face\"}"
